9. fixing CORS errors

What is preflight request?”
A preflight request is an HTTP OPTIONS request sent by the browser before certain
cross-origin requests to check if the server allows the actual request based on method, headers, and origin.

 # ✅ HANDLE PREFLIGHT
    if ($request_method = OPTIONS) {
        add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin "https://student.unemployengineer.works";
        add_header Access-Control-Allow-Credentials "true";
        add_header Access-Control-Allow-Methods "GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS";
        add_header Access-Control-Allow-Headers "Content-Type, Authorization";
        return 204;
    }